From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: rpivid: allow cache hints on the CAPTURE queue

Lets a program ask for cacheable decoded frames with
V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT (vb2 then cleans and invalidates them
at QBUF and DQBUF). ReelHWAccel's hevcdec under RISC OS on Linux reads
frames with the CPU; write-combined frames converted 3-4 times slower
than native. The OUTPUT queue is unchanged.
---
--- a/drivers/staging/media/rpivid/rpivid_video.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/rpivid/rpivid_video.c
@@ -686,6 +686,10 @@
 	dst_vq->timestamp_flags = V4L2_BUF_FLAG_TIMESTAMP_COPY;
 	dst_vq->lock = &ctx->ctx_mutex;
 	dst_vq->dev = ctx->dev->dev;
+	/* RISC OS on Linux: cacheable frames on request (CREATE_BUFS/REQBUFS
+	 * with V4L2_MEMORY_FLAG_NON_COHERENT), so ReelHWAccel's hevcdec can
+	 * read decoded pictures with the CPU at native speed. */
+	dst_vq->allow_cache_hints = 1;
 
 	return vb2_queue_init(dst_vq);
 }
